ppc64le: configure's `check_inline_asm ppc4xx '"maclhw…"'` probe
false-positives under the engine (clang's native asm parser accepts the
PPC405/440 `maclhw`/`mullhw` even for a POWER8 target), so it sets
HAVE_PPC4XX=1 and this header emits those embedded-only MACs, which ld.lld's
stricter LTO codegen then rejects as invalid. `--disable-ppc4xx` only clears
CONFIG_PPC4XX, not the HAVE_ capability the header guards on, so neutralize the
guard here (the only maclhw/mullhw users in the tree). POWER8 is not a 4xx
core, so this is a misdetection fix, not a feature loss.

--- a/libavcodec/ppc/mathops.h
+++ b/libavcodec/ppc/mathops.h
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "libavutil/common.h"
 
-#if HAVE_PPC4XX
+#if 0
 /* signed 16x16 -> 32 multiply add accumulate */
 #define MAC16(rt, ra, rb) \
     __asm__ ("maclhw %0, %2, %3" : "=r" (rt) : "0" (rt), "r" (ra), "r" (rb));
